  "draw": "census: all 95 witnesses of census.json, in order",
  "transcript": "Canonical serialization rule: take the proposal artifact EXACTLY as given in the prompt, serialize it as JSON with sorted keys and no whitespace, and persist the exact bytes hashed as proposal_canon.json in the run scratch dir; compute hProposal = SHA-256(proposal_canon.json) and then compute seed = SHA-256(hProposal + salt) where salt is the instance-provided salt (3f7f7c0eb4b706de325c013e4e217ce8afe8d84a0135aa176e591dda3260d5a2); a third party can re-derive by hashing proposal_canon.json to reproduce hProposal, then hashing hProposal concatenated with the same salt to reproduce the provided seedHex, and can verify the canonical bytes by checking sha256sum proposal_canon.json equals hProposal."
